<urn:usf:requirement:job-lifecycle-dedup-currentness:2> <urn:usf:predicate:objective> "eventKey is exact over job/work/attempt/phase/eventKind. Start and terminal event kinds have separate keys. Identical replay deduplicates, conflicting same-key facts refuse, and final logical attempt aggregates once." <urn:usf:graph:job-lifecycle-metrics-v2> .
<urn:usf:requirement:job-lifecycle-dedup-currentness:2> <urn:usf:predicate:failureMode> "Negative or unsafe-integer offsets/durations, unmatched terminal/start pair, conflicting duplicate, or unaccounted parent-child overlap refuses. Nested intervals are never summed automatically. A focused reader invariant requires one clockDomainIdentity, endOffset >= startOffset, endOffset-startOffset = duration, and compares monotonic offsets only within that domain; UTC startedAt/finishedAt are observations, never duration inputs." <urn:usf:graph:job-lifecycle-metrics-v2> .
